% You are an expert Python engineer. Define regenerate_dag.

<include>context/project_preamble.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Restructures the DAG after a node state change using MiniMax, orchestrated via the RocketRide pipeline.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "module",
  "module": {
    "functions": [
      {
        "name": "regenerate_dag",
        "signature": "(current_dag: list[DAGNode], mem0_state: dict) -> list[DAGNode]",
        "returns": "list[DAGNode] — same nodes, updated status and ordering"
      }
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Accepts the full current DAG JSON and the full mem0 state, and returns an updated DAG with
reordered recommendations, newly unlocked nodes, and updated priorities based on what the user
has actually mastered. Runs whenever the RocketRide pipeline delivers a `content.classified` or
`node.mastered` event; publishes `dag.regenerated` on success.

Two-phase approach:
1. LLM call: asks MiniMax to reorder and update statuses. If the LLM call fails for any reason,
   fall back to a deep copy of current_dag before applying the belt-and-suspenders rules below.
2. Belt-and-suspenders enforcement (always applied, regardless of LLM success/failure):
   - R1: any nodes the LLM dropped are appended from current_dag.
   - R3: prerequisite edges are restored from current_dag.
   - R4: immutable fields (id, title, description, success_criteria) are restored from current_dag.
   - R5: mastered nodes are locked in to their mastered status and completed_at.
   - R8: seen nodes are preserved — `_normalize_statuses` skips them to prevent regression.
   - R2/R9: a final pass unlocks every locked node whose all prerequisites are mastered.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- Does not classify content or score comprehension.
- Does not add new top-level topics — only restructures the existing DAG.
- Does not write to Postgres (the caller persists the result).
- Does not write to mem0.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
- Unlocked node: a node whose prerequisites have all transitioned to status `mastered`.
- mem0_state: the full user memory object from mem0, including completed node IDs, completion timestamps, content format preferences, and learning pace.
- Reordering: changing the recommended next-node priority based on what was just mastered and the user's observed learning pace — not changing prerequisite relationships.
- seen node: a node the user has visited a learning resource for; status is between "available" and "mastered". Must not regress to "available" during regeneration.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Return every node from the input DAG — never drop nodes.
R2 (MUST): Unlock every node whose prerequisites are all mastered in the returned DAG. Enforced by the final programmatic pass after LLM output validation.
R3 (MUST): Preserve all prerequisite relationships exactly as received — never add or remove edges.
R4 (MUST NOT): Change any node's id, title, description, or success_criteria fields.
R5 (MUST NOT): Change the status of a mastered node to any other status.
R6 (MUST): Use mem0_state.completed_at timestamps to infer learning pace and reorder available nodes by estimated fit.
R7 (MUST NOT): Invent new nodes — only update existing ones.
R8 (MUST NOT): Change a seen node's status to "available" — seen is ≥ available and must not regress. `_normalize_statuses` skips nodes whose status is "seen" or "mastered".
R9 (MUST): If the LLM call raises any exception, fall back to a deep copy of current_dag and apply the same belt-and-suspenders rules. The fallback must still satisfy R1–R8.
</contract_rules>

<capabilities>
- MAY call MiniMax LLM API.
- MAY read mem0_state (read-only).
- MAY subscribe to `content.classified` and `node.mastered` RocketRide events.
- MAY publish `dag.regenerated` on success.
- MUST NOT write to mem0.
- MUST NOT call Rtrvr.ai or ElevenLabs.
- MUST NOT write to Postgres.
- MUST NOT call another agent's function directly.
</capabilities>

<coverage>
R1: story__regenerate_dag_no_nodes_lost.md
R2: story__regenerate_dag_unlocks_dependants.md
R3: story__regenerate_dag_no_nodes_lost.md
R4: TODO add dedicated field-immutability story before production use
R5: story__regenerate_dag_no_regression.md
R6: TODO add dedicated pace-reordering story before production use
R7: story__regenerate_dag_no_nodes_lost.md
R8: story__seen_node_cannot_regress.md
R9: TODO add dedicated llm-fallback story before production use
</coverage>
